{"year":"2021","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 74th Cannes Film Festival took place from July 6 to 17, 2021, postponed from May due to the COVID-19 pandemic, a year after the 2020 edition was canceled. The jury was presided over by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 5281, 'screen_type': person}\">Spike Lee</a>, the first Black person to hold the post, and the opening film was <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 424277, 'screen_type': movie}\">Annette</a> (2021), which earned <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 27977, 'screen_type': person}\">Leos Carax</a> the directing prize. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 630240, 'screen_type': movie}\">Titane</a> (2021) gave the Palme d'Or to <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1392433, 'screen_type': person}\">Julia Ducournau</a>, the second woman to win the award and the first to win it alone (in 1993, Jane Campion shared the Palme with Chen Kaige). At the closing ceremony, Spike Lee mistakenly announced the Palme winner right at the start of the evening."},{"type":"person_list","title":"The Jury","persons":[{"id":5281,"name":"Spike Lee","profile_path":"/2KOHXgk2uoRXl6u7V9xpAIo3uay.jpg"},{"id":136168,"name":"Mati Diop","profile_path":"/3p8euc4PO9Yo9RR0PjaADsN9R6V.jpg"},{"id":145755,"name":"Mylène Farmer","profile_path":"/p5U9gpQu1uO1pDiBET56ASmwb4j.jpg"},{"id":1579,"name":"Maggie Gyllenhaal","profile_path":"/vsfkWdYWmA9CpzMHTJzrFxlDnEZ.jpg"},{"id":19896,"name":"Jessica Hausner","profile_path":"/ZnNp71lxHD4lv5kB6i1pN6K58h.jpg"},{"id":19119,"name":"Mélanie Laurent","profile_path":"/i99ogEo4gQyanCmHWYYoS6hsUqL.jpg"},{"id":1016214,"name":"Kleber Mendonça Filho","profile_path":"/7jOzp98FiL6C22tphTHEPWAhK11.jpg"},{"id":81051,"name":"Tahar Rahim","profile_path":"/r1SJ9nkG9q4JbPHbtcvcVxmRcHw.jpg"},{"id":20738,"name":"Song Kang-ho","profile_path":"/kBM9UTPYXUA2RNk210DXhztLFns.jpg"}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Palme d'Or","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":630240,"name":"Titane"